				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Enhance text search with column highlighting and fix extension config loading\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing significant search UX improvements:\n\n1. Mountain (44bf29d4):\n   - Fix extension config loading: previously searched for non-existent VS Code manifest shape ([{key, value}]), causing extensions like vscode.git to activate but never reach createSourceControl(). Now walks both array AND object shapes, extracts default values using dotted keys (e.g. git.enabled).\n   - Add ColumnRange tracking so Sky can underline actual match positions instead of whole lines\n   - Fix line numbers: previously returned 0, now returns 1-based\n   - Add byte→char map with binary search for O(log n) UTF-8 column lookups (previously O(n) per match, causing quadratic slowdown on match-dense files)\n   - Cap preview at 512 chars to avoid massive layouts on minified files\n   - Add per-line match cap (100) to prevent hangs on pathological regexes\n\n2. Sky (61849605):\n   - Parse Mountain's columns array (0-based UTF-8 char offsets) and transform into VS Code's 1-based ISearchRange format\n   - Populate preview.matches with preview-local coordinates so renderer shows precise character-level highlighting\n   - Previously all matches displayed as full-line highlights with no sub-line underline\n\nImpact: Text search results now show precise character-level match highlighting, extension configuration properly loads defaults, and large file searches perform significantly better.",
			"SHA": "adba2d4ab64268bb23038ff0a593a2c85d4d54fb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T09:59:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Sync Sky and Cocoon submodules to fix search result handling\n\nRoutine submodule synchronization bringing in critical bug fixes:\n\n1. Sky (a3139802):\n   - Fix text search result mapping to use Mountain's actual response format: `Hit.resource` instead of `Hit.uri`, and `Hit.matches[]` array (with `preview` and `line_number`) instead of flat hit shape\n   - Add backwards-compat support for old flat `{uri, lineNumber, preview}` format\n   - Fix search:findFiles IPC call to include required null exclude parameter - previously MaxResults shifted into wrong slot, causing glob extractor to ignore max and default to 10000\n   - This resolves empty search results where previous code produced resource=MakeFileUri(\"\") with empty results array\n\n2. Cocoon (f0ec9445):\n   - Submodule sync to latest extension host changes\n\nImpact: Text search and file search now return correct results using Mountain's response format.",
